Open Terminal (press ⌘ + Space, type Terminal, then press Return).

/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"

Enter your Mac password

The installation may take a few minutes.

brew --version

it should come up Homebrew 4.x.x

If you get brew: command not found
Run the command Homebrew tells you to add it to your PATH. On most Apple Silicon Macs, it's:

echo 'eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"' >> ~/.zprofile
eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"

